<title>DENMARK: SAS down five percent on Q1 loss.</title>
<headline>SAS down five percent on Q1 loss.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) shares fell five percent on the Copenhagen Stock Exchange on Wednesday, following Tuesday's announcement of a 269 Swedish crown first quarter loss.</p>
<p>At 0925 GMT the share was down 3.50 Danish crowns, to 66.50.</p>
<p>Announcing the loss on Tuesday, which compared to a profit of 311 million Swedish crowns in the first quarter of 1996, SAS said it still stood by a forecast for full-year 1997 profits similar to last year's 1.815 billion Swedish crowns.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
